Massachusetts it's ready to send its  first black Democrat to Congress after  another high-profile election upset  Boston City Council Anna Presley is her  name she won the Democratic nomination  in the state's seventh congressional  district primary last night she defeated  congressman Michael Capuano who was a  20-year incumbent at O'Keefe is on  Capitol Hill with the latest shake-up  for the establishment Democrats at good  morning this is big news there in  Massachusetts big news in Boston Gala  surprised virtually everyone including  the candidate herself video taken by one  of her staffers showed a reaction to the  news last night many are drawing  comparisons between Presley's win and  that of New York Democrat Alexandria  Ocasio Cortez who back in June defeated  another longtime Democratic congressman  but while Ocasio Cortez ran to the left  of her opponent Presley and Congressman  Mike Capuano actually didn't have too  many differences he's been a reliable  liberal over the course of his 20 years  in Congress but his Presley put it  recently it's not just good enough to  have Democrats back in power  it matters who those Democrats are  Presley is now one of a handful of  mostly female minority liberals who are  winning races across the country  Connecticut for example has probably  going to elect its first black female  congresswoman to Congress in November  down in Georgia Stacey Abrams is running  for governor  Andrew Gilliam of course won a primary  last week in Florida while Presley is  running unopposed however people like  Abrams and Gilliam may struggle to  convince general election voters this  November to support Norah a black woman  now representing a seat held by Joe  Kennedy and JFK jr. ed thanks so much
 

